+
+### 3.3 `release-prepare.yml` — immutable candidate preparation
+
+Triggers: a `v*` tag push or explicit `workflow_dispatch` by a trusted
+maintainer. Both triggers merely request preparation; neither authorizes a
+release. Preparation loads workflow code from the protected default branch and
+resolves the requested ref to an exact reachable commit.
+
+| Job / blocking check | Actor trust and input | Token / environment / secrets | Network | Outputs / retention | Approval |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `release/candidate-identity` | Trusted trigger; exact default-branch commit, signed/annotated tag metadata if present, declared version | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | GitHub metadata read only | Immutable candidate manifest and tag/ref evidence; release-record/7y | None |
+| `release/revalidate` | Exact candidate manifest | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | Same allowlists as credential-free CI | Fresh results for every active required check, with digests | None |
+| `release/review-gate` | Exact manifest plus complete active evidence index | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | Deny | Machine verdict: promotable/non-promotable/unknown; release-record/7y | Recorded engineering/security/release approvals; human ratification remains `TASK-260717-2d308k` before publication |
+
+The candidate manifest records source commit, clean-state assertion, source and
+dependency locks, toolchain/SDK/runner images, protocol and relay manifests,
+marketing/build versions, expected artifact names, and every evidence digest.
+It is immutable after `release/review-gate` starts.
+
