 ### 2215 — Architecture matrix review requests deterministic harness-test rework (TASK-260715-nphtib)
 - VERIFICATION: Independent `--no-hardlinks` detached-clone validation at `7dc73ac6e7325f86a4a178a0558619f0fc9d1490` passed the repository credential-free matrix (exit 0, 417.04s), strict formatting, 89.96% product-line coverage, exact macOS graph, double generation, unsigned Debug/Release bundle/linkage inspection, relay checksums, and pinned legacy regression. No signing, installation, application/provider launch, VPN preference/tunnel, route, or DNS operation ran.
 - REVIEW FINDING: The same revision has a recorded real `swift test` failure in `HarnessTests.cancellationCleanup` (`TimedOut()` at line 140), while the test still uses a scheduler-count loop of 10,000 `Task.yield()` calls. The new clean matrix, coverage run, and 50 targeted repeats passed, but they do not invalidate the observed nondeterministic failure or prove the unchanged race is eliminated.
 - VERDICT: Changes requested under the explicit deterministic-test gate. `BUG-260819-34ikhl` remains the concrete rework item: reproduce under repetition/load, replace the scheduler-count timeout without weakening cleanup assertions, then prove repeated clean full-suite and coverage passes before a fresh review.
 
 ### 0520 — Harness cancellation readiness is event-synchronized (BUG-260819-34ikhl)
 - ROOT CAUSE: `HarnessTests.cancellationCleanup` treated 10,000 executor yields as a deadline for the command task to acquire `ResourceRecorder` and publish ownership. Under loaded Swift Testing execution the waiter could exhaust scheduler turns before the command ran, producing `TimedOut()` even though no resource-cleanup invariant had failed.
 - FIX: The recorder now resumes checked continuations when the command has registered its temporary directory, Unix socket, and managed task. Cancellation is delivered only after that explicit ownership event; no sleep, retry, timeout increase, or weakened assertion remains. The production task group continues to cancel and join both children before the actor-owned resource scope performs its guarded reverse-order cleanup.
 - VERIFICATION: The focused test runs 50 parameterized cases concurrently and asserts exit 143, empty output, removed directory/socket, and exactly one managed-task cancellation. Three clean full `swift test` runs passed 443 tests in 81.63s, 80.87s, and 83.88s; coverage passed 443 tests in 83.06s. Strict recursive Swift formatting, `git diff --check`, core boundaries, and full `make credential-free-validate` passed. Only the existing 25 ReluxNIOSSH-unavailable known issues were reported; no signing, installation, launch, VPN/network preference, route, or DNS mutation ran.
 
 ### 0530 — Harness cancellation readiness review finds an unbounded startup-failure waiter (BUG-260819-34ikhl)
 - REVIEW FINDING: `ResourceRecorder.waitUntilStarted()` registers a non-throwing checked continuation that is resumed only by `record(directory:socket:)`. Any command error before that publication (temporary-directory creation, marker write, socket creation/bind, or managed-task registration) makes `HarnessApplication.run` finish with `commandFailed`, while `cancellationCleanup` remains suspended before it can join `run.value`. The waiter has no command-completion, cancellation, or bounded diagnostic path, so it can leak and hang the test indefinitely.
 - VERIFICATION: The normal success path remains strong: 50 parameterized cases under four CPU-load workers passed in 0.018s, a clean full suite passed 443 tests in 37 suites, and coverage passed the same 443 tests; strict Swift format, core-boundary, diff, and board gates all exited 0. These green paths do not exercise the identified pre-readiness failure transition.
 - VERDICT: Changes requested. Preserve the actor-atomic check/register and exact cleanup assertions, but make readiness a terminal event state that also completes waiters on command startup failure/cancellation, and add deterministic regression coverage proving that path cannot hang or retain a waiter.
 
